# Gonti, Night Minister and Walking Corpse (both cast on turn 1 with Black Lotus and three Mox Jets) attack Bot2 on turn 3 and
# both connect: the trigger is "whenever a creature deals combat damage to one of your opponents", so each creature makes its
# own (Bot2 takes 3 + 2 = 5, and two cards leave the top of its library face down: Plains and Ornithopter, 12 -> 10). Bot1, as
# each creature's controller, plays the exiled Plains as its land for the turn and casts the exiled Ornithopter for {0}; the
# Ornithopter is a spell Bot1 does not own, so Bot1 gets one Treasure. Bot1's own fourth Mox Jet, cast with Gonti out, is a
# spell Bot1 owns and makes no Treasure - the single Treasure Token on the battlefield is the proof.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Gonti, Night Minister
Walking Corpse
Mox Jet
Swamp x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x8
Plains
Ornithopter
Island x10

